{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"86372cbd4b76439edb9041576abb7dfc01d63bf176d0f30946645635dc750c60","digest":{"component_or_area":"bridge suggest-mapping command","key_entities":["rebar bridge suggest-mapping","mapping_probe.py","mapping_config.py","src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/bridge.py","src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","_bridge_suggest_mapping","_config_writer._emit_nested_toml","_config_writer._emit_config_toml","jira.JIRA.issue_types","jira.JIRA.priorities","jira.JIRA.issue_link_types","jira.JIRA.statuses","jira.JIRA.createmeta_issuetypes","jira.JIRA.search_issues","jira.JIRA.transitions","rebar.toml","tool.rebar.mapping","issue_types","statuses","link_types","hierarchy","priority_map","status_map","type_map","link_map","create_defaults","tomllib"],"problem_keywords":["mapping configuration","jira probe","vocabulary discovery","live jira","toml serialization","axis mapping"],"propositions":["A new read-only CLI command `rebar bridge suggest-mapping <PROJECT>` probes a live Jira instance via pycontribs client to discover actual issue types, statuses, link types, priorities, and hierarchy levels.","The command emits a suggested `[tool.rebar.mapping]` block with discovered vocabulary and identity-seeded axis maps to stdout by default, never modifying files unless `--write` is specified.","When `--write` is used, the command performs deep-merge of discovered mapping under existing `rebar.toml` or creates one, preserving hand-edited values and flat `[jira]`/`[tracker]` sections while avoiding mutation of `pyproject.toml`.","Transition hints are discovered by sampling one issue per type and reading its available transitions from the current status, explicitly flagged as best-effort/partial since Jira returns only current-status transitions.","A new TOML orchestrator splits flat and nested serialization: `_emit_config_toml` handles top-level siblings via the existing `_emit_toml` and delegates nested `[mapping.*]` sub-tables to `_emit_nested_toml`, preserving the fail-closed contract of the original emitter.","The probe is fully offline-testable via a fake port returning canned data, with no live Jira credentials or CI gating required for test execution."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787768883184053001,"uuid":"104feacd-bd82-42e5-89ef-f58585a73a67"}